# General
.DS_Store

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# JetBrains project files (per-machine, not repo content)
.idea/

# AuditGame experiment outputs - regenerate with `python3 experiment.py --json`
auditgame/*.json
!auditgame/reference/score_table.json

# AuditGame SWE-bench metadata (~54 MB) - reproducible via `swebench_fetch.py`
auditgame/data/*.jsonl

# AuditGame harness roots (harness.py).  Repo clones, the four carriers, the
# generated hidden suites and the sealed area are RUN ARTEFACTS: workspace/ holds
# third-party repos with their own .git, carriers/ is per-run state,
# hidden_suites/ is the answer key, and carriers-sealed/ is the OTHER answer key
# -- the per-item `poisoned` labels and the sealed manifests, which Task 19 moved
# out of carriers/ precisely so the agent cannot read them.  Committing it would
# publish the ground truth this benchmark exists to infer.  None of the four
# belongs in this repo.
auditgame/workspace/
auditgame/carriers/
auditgame/carriers-sealed/
auditgame/hidden_suites/
# The container ground-truth probe (tests/gate1_integrity/
# test_ground_truth_out_of_the_carriers.py) makes `probe-XXXXXX/` under the same
# directory, because the Docker daemon may be a VM whose file-sharing list covers
# the project and not the system temp dir.  A killed run leaves one behind holding
# a carrier root, a SEALED AREA WITH LABELS and a git repo -- the same three things
# the four lines above keep out of the repo.
auditgame/probe-*/

# `results/` is deliberately NOT ignored, and the asymmetry with the four roots
# above is the point -- but the trace itself is SPLIT ON THE SAME SEAL LINE, and
# only its public half is committed.
#
# `results/M3-trace.json` is Task 17's named deliverable and the input every
# offline replay reads; it is never mounted into a container, and the acceptance
# line it has to meet -- "the trace carries all nine field groups of SPEC-P1b
# Part 1" -- is a claim a reviewer can only check against a committed file.  That
# claim is about the trace's SHAPE.  The file used to carry its LABELS too: a
# `poisoned` flag on every item record, the planted payload's whole record under
# `injected`, and a `correct` verdict beside every quarantine -- the ground truth
# for every item plus whether each quarantine was right.  Committing that is the
# same act this file refuses two paragraphs up, arriving through the deliverable
# instead of through the store.  So `core.dump_traces` now writes two files and
# the answer key goes to `results/M3-sealed.json`, which is ignored HERE, beside
# `carriers-sealed/`, for the same reason and in the same words: publishing it
# would hand over the labels the benchmark exists to infer.
#
# What is committed, and what a reader therefore gets: every task's before/after
# carrier snapshot, every write's content, provenance and timestamp, every state
# query and what came back, every raw alarm score, the live count per carrier, the
# P1..P5 checkpoints, which items were quarantined, the public/hidden verdicts and
# the measured audit seconds.  What is not: which of those items was planted, which
# writes inherited from it, and which quarantine was right.
#
# `sealed_trace.load` is the reader that puts the two halves together, and it
# REFUSES when the sealed half is absent rather than returning traces on which
# nothing is poisoned -- a full grid of Rule N3 fake zeros is the failure mode this
# split would otherwise buy.
auditgame/results/*-sealed.json

# Khoá API — .env chứa DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, không bao giờ commit.
.env
# Cache của understand-anything, sinh lại được.
.ua/
